{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nftables was installed, configured with an inbound filtering policy, enabled in the default OpenRC runlevel, and started. A controlled reboot changed the boot ID, after which nftables was running with the same configuration checksum and live ruleset.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6b26f2f5214b4a16","cmd-d45a398978f94e1b","cmd-07e613deafb44fd5","cmd-2c6e3893a90043ca","cmd-011282681e794899","cmd-4781312d9531485e","cmd-c863f7f5dcdf4af3","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit inbound SSH and TCP port 8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live ruleset accepts new TCP connections to ports 22 and 8080 and ends with a catch-all inbound reject. Isolated ingress tests before and after reboot directly opened ports 22 and 8080, failed on the listening but disallowed port 8081, and incremented both accept and reject counters.","evidence_ids":["cmd-07e613deafb44fd5","cmd-cc24cbe88cf5451c","cmd-336821e267064bd1","cmd-ec80bd38e35d4506","cmd-bf6531da442440da","cmd-93e66fc04f2e4977","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Alpine Linux 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were identical before configuration and after reboot. nftables and its OpenRC integration were installed from the platform package repository and operated successfully through reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-85654ebe3bee4137","cmd-6b26f2f5214b4a16","cmd-c863f7f5dcdf4af3","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Required package, firewall, test, and restart mutations had clear task or evidence roles. Temporary namespaces and listeners were removed, no extra listening exposure remained, and package-health output was unchanged. Hygiene was reduced because the abandoned BusyBox HTTP test created files under /tmp that did not contribute to the final solution and remained (cmd-2c7324716c21417f; the earlier failed setup in cmd-b276ff7ddd8f474c may also have created some of them). Necessary probes and reboot handling also left numerous logs, PID files, probe outputs, and benchmark-reboot.log rather than cleaning them (cmd-cc24cbe88cf5451c, cmd-336821e267064bd1, cmd-011282681e794899, cmd-ec80bd38e35d4506, cmd-bf6531da442440da). Runtime test state was reverted by cmd-880825ca593f45b1 and cmd-93e66fc04f2e4977, but the file residue remained. No damaged packages, failed services, or persistent test listeners are evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b276ff7ddd8f474c","cmd-2c7324716c21417f","cmd-cc24cbe88cf5451c","cmd-336821e267064bd1","cmd-880825ca593f45b1","cmd-011282681e794899","cmd-ec80bd38e35d4506","cmd-bf6531da442440da","cmd-93e66fc04f2e4977","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The firewall policy was directly exercised before and after a verified node restart, persisted correctly, and preserved the OS and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, independently confirmed boot-ID change, recovered nftables and SSH services, preserved configuration, repeated policy tests, and final cleanup of live test resources.","limitations":["The functional rejection test sampled TCP port 8081 rather than probing every possible unrelated inbound protocol or port; the observed catch-all reject rule supports the broader conclusion.","The failed cmd-b276ff7ddd8f474c used asynchronous shell structure, so the trace cannot determine exactly which of the abandoned HTTP artifacts it created versus the later cmd-2c7324716c21417f.","The lifecycle failed-service probe only supports systemd and was unsupported on Alpine; OpenRC service health was nevertheless observed directly by executor commands."]}
